    <node id="Eiffel Tower">
      <data key="d0">Eiffel Tower</data>
      <data key="d1">landmark</data>
      <data key="d2">**The Eiffel Tower: A Timeless Symbol of French Culture and Engineering**

The Eiffel Tower, situated in the heart of Paris, France, is a renowned landmark that has become synonymous with the City of Light. This iconic structure, standing as one of the most recognizable symbols of French culture and engineering prowess, was initially intended as a temporary installation for the 1889 World's Fair but has since become an enduring symbol of French heritage and innovation.

Located in Paris, the capital city of France, the Eiffel Tower is a global center for art, fashion, cuisine, and entertainment. The tower's presence in this historic city adds to its allure, drawing millions of visitors each year who come to marvel at its sheer scale and beauty. As the most-visited paid monument in the world, the Eiffel Tower is an integral part of Paris's cultural landscape.

Standing at 324 meters tall, the Eiffel Tower is a testament to French engineering and architectural evolution. Its design and construction have made it a staple of Parisian identity, reflecting the city's rich history and cultural significance. The tower has inspired generations with its elegance and grandeur, solidifying its place as one of the world's most beloved landmarks.

While not explicitly mentioned in every description, it is worth noting that Eiffel Tower shares the same name as another entity in a different location. However, for the purpose of this summary, we will focus on the Parisian landmark.</data>
