    <node id="France">
      <data key="d0">France</data>
      <data key="d1">country</data>
      <data key="d2">France is a location in Europe where Emmanuel Macron serves as the President. As the head of state, Macron has been instrumental in shaping the country's policies and direction. France is a significant player on the global stage, known for its rich history, cultural heritage, and contributions to various fields such as art, science, and philosophy.

The country has a diverse geography, featuring a mix of mountainous regions, coastal areas, and fertile plains. France is also home to many notable cities, including Paris, Lyon, Marseille, and Bordeaux, each with its own unique character and attractions. The French economy is one of the largest in the world, driven by industries such as manufacturing, finance, and tourism.

In addition to Macron's leadership, France has a long history of influential figures who have shaped the country's development. From the medieval era to the present day, France has been home to numerous renowned artists, writers, philosophers, and scientists who have left an indelible mark on human knowledge and culture.</data>
