    <node id="Apple">
      <data key="d0">Apple</data>
      <data key="d1">company</data>
      <data key="d2">Apple, a multinational technology and consumer electronics company, was founded on April 1, 1976, by Steve Jobs, Steve Wozniak, and Ronald Wayne. Initially focused on making personal computers, Apple's first product was the Apple I, which was later followed by the Apple II, one of the first highly successful mass-produced personal computers.

Throughout its history, Apple has been at the forefront of technological innovation, introducing revolutionary products such as the Macintosh computer in 1984 and the iPod portable music player in 2001. The company's transition to mobile devices with the iPhone in 2007 marked a significant shift in its focus and was followed by the introduction of the iPad tablet in 2010.

Today, Apple is one of the world's largest and most influential technology companies, known for its sleek and user-friendly designs, as well as its commitment to innovation and customer satisfaction. Although initially focused on making personal computers, Apple has expanded its product line to include a range of mobile devices and accessories, from Mac computers to AirPods wireless earbuds.

It is worth noting that while some descriptions referred to Apple simply as "Company" or "Technology," the company's official name and primary focus are indeed centered around technology and consumer electronics.&lt;SEP&gt;Company&lt;SEP&gt;Technology&lt;SEP&gt;tech`&lt;SEP&gt;tech&lt;SEP&gt;USA</data>
