    <node id="Larry Page">
      <data key="d0">Larry Page</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Larry Page is a prominent figure in the technology industry. He was born on March 26, 1973, and is best known for co-founding Google with Sergey Brin while he was a Ph.D. student at Stanford University in California. As of the latest information available to me as of my knowledge cutoff date in 2023, Larry Page has served as the Chief Executive Officer (CEO) of Alphabet Inc., the parent company of Google, since 2015. However, he stepped down from this position in December 2020 and became the CEO of Alphabet's holding subsidiary, Alphabet Holdings LLC.

Page received his undergraduate degree in engineering from the University of Michigan in 1995 and later pursued a Master's degree in computer science at Stanford before dropping out to focus on Google full-time. He has been recognized with numerous awards for his innovative work in the field of computer science and technology, including the Marconi Society Prize.

In addition to his professional achievements, Larry Page is also known for his philanthropic efforts, particularly through his charitable organization, The Carl Victor Page Memorial Fund. This foundation focuses on providing support to various causes, ranging from education and healthcare to scientific research and environmental conservation.

Note: Given the repetitive descriptions in the input list, I have condensed them into a single summary that maintains the key information without exceeding the token limit of 600 tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;/en</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ba3e90c2d1072a112c64a2e945249a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8c7768f569b60243c23f6ee51f14db0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
