    </node>
    <node id="Sergey Brin">
      <data key="d0">Sergey Brin</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Sergey Brin, a renowned entrepreneur and computer scientist, is best known as the co-founder of Google. Born in Russia, Sergey Brin's name is often rendered in its original Cyrillic form (/ru). His Russian heritage is a significant aspect of his identity.

Growing up in Moscow, Sergey was fascinated by mathematics and computing from an early age. He later moved to the United States with his family, where he attended the University of Maryland and graduated with a degree in mathematics and computer science. At Stanford University, Brin met Larry Page, and together they began working on a research project that would eventually become Google.

Sergey's involvement with Google was not limited to its founding; he has also held various leadership positions within the company, including serving as President of Technology from 2015 until 2020. During his tenure, Brin oversaw significant technological advancements and expansions in artificial intelligence, cloud computing, and cybersecurity.

Brin has received numerous awards for his contributions to technology and entrepreneurship. In recognition of his impact on modern society, he was appointed a fellow of the American Academy of Arts and Sciences. His work at Google has also earned him numerous accolades, including the National Medal of Technology and Innovation in 2008.

Throughout his career, Sergey Brin has been an advocate for transparency and accountability in technology. He has spoken out on issues related to digital rights, cybersecurity, and the responsible use of artificial intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;/ru</data>
